9.3.1
# The first line of this file is used by Bazelisk and Bazel to be sure
# the right version of Bazel is used to build and test this repo.
# This also defines which version is used on CI. Since the root
# .bazelrc pins --lockfile_mode=error, bump this in lockstep with
# MODULE.bazel.lock (regenerate it with the new version via
# `bazel mod deps --lockfile_mode=update`) so strict runs below and
# BuildBuddy stay consistent with the committed lockfile.
#
# Note that you should also run the e2e workspaces against other Bazel
# versions you support.
